    "order": "family given",
    "conventions": "Korean names put the one-syllable family name first and a two-syllable given name after it: Kim Min-jun. A handful of family names cover most people (Kim, Lee, Park, Choi, Jung). Women keep their own family name when they marry. Names are written here in their usual Latin spellings (Lee rather than I, Park rather than Bak), with the given name hyphenated. Strangers and colleagues use the full name or family name plus -ssi or a job title (Kim gwajangnim), and many people working with foreigners also use an English name.",
